; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Spinning Squares
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     repeat, rotation, color, square
; SUMMARY:  Draws one square, turns a little, draws another, until a ring of colored squares makes a flower.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A square is drawn 36 times. Between squares the turtle turns 10
;   degrees, and the pen color changes. Together the squares make a
;   round, flower-like pattern. A second, smaller pattern in the
;   middle is made the same way with fewer squares.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then try  spin 12 100  or  spin 72 150  yourself.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * repeat a shape and turn: the most famous Logo pattern trick
;   * 36 squares x 10 degrees = 360, a full turn
;   * REPCOUNT counts the times round the loop; we use it for color
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 20 squares. How far must the turtle turn between them?
;   * Change SQUARE to draw a triangle instead.
;   * Make each square a little bigger than the last one.
; ============================================================

to square :size
  repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]
end

; Draw :copies squares, turning an equal share of 360 degrees
; after each one so the last square ends where the first began.
to spin :copies :size
  repeat :copies [
    setpencolor item 1 + remainder repcount 6 [[230 50 50] [240 140 0] [230 200 0] [40 160 70] [40 110 220] [140 60 190]]
    square :size
    right 360 / :copies
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 35]
setpensize 2
spin 36 180
setpensize 3
spin 12 60
